Z||000029||Eric||05-22-2001||11:32 PM||||I just want to go on the record as saying I have plenty of respect and admiration for anyone of any sex who works on their own car.  I for one am not the type to get all dirty and greasy turning wrenchs.  It's just not my cup.  There are plenty of people out there ready and willing to take my money to work on my machine.  I find it ironic that men spend (waste) half of their money on women and half on cars in order to impress women.  I believe men like me would rather pay a woman to work on our car than a man if only because we feel that entering another man into this whole money/car/women equation would just serve to confuse us, and with our simple, primative minds, only bad things could result, not to mention the inevitable sexual confusion.  By the way Veronica, my hands are like a little girl's  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
